# What is a Stored Procedure?

A Stored Procedure is a collection of SQL statements stored inside the database. It can be executed whenever required.

It improves:
- Performance
- Code Reusability
- Security
- Maintainability

---

# Basic Syntax

```sql
DELIMITER $$

CREATE PROCEDURE ProcedureName()
BEGIN

    SQL Statements;

END $$

DELIMITER ;
```

---

# Execute Procedure

```sql
CALL ProcedureName();
```

---

# Example

```sql
DELIMITER $$

CREATE PROCEDURE GetStudents()
BEGIN

    SELECT * FROM Student;

END $$

DELIMITER ;
```

Execute

```sql
CALL GetStudents();
```

---

# Procedure with IN Parameter

```sql
DELIMITER $$

CREATE PROCEDURE GetStudentById
(
    IN pId INT
)
BEGIN

    SELECT *
    FROM Student
    WHERE Id = pId;

END $$

DELIMITER ;
```

Execute

```sql
CALL GetStudentById(2);
```

---

# INSERT Procedure

```sql
DELIMITER $$

CREATE PROCEDURE InsertStudent
(
    IN pName VARCHAR(100),
    IN pAge INT,
    IN pScore INT
)
BEGIN

    INSERT INTO Student(Name,Age,Score)
    VALUES(pName,pAge,pScore);

END $$

DELIMITER ;
```

Execute

```sql
CALL InsertStudent('Rahul',22,90);
```

---

# UPDATE Procedure

```sql
DELIMITER $$

CREATE PROCEDURE UpdateStudent
(
    IN pId INT,
    IN pName VARCHAR(100),
    IN pScore INT
)
BEGIN

    UPDATE Student
    SET
        Name = pName,
        Score = pScore
    WHERE Id = pId;

END $$

DELIMITER ;
```

Execute

```sql
CALL UpdateStudent(1,'Ruturaj',98);
```

