# IN Parameter

Input value comes from the caller.

```sql
IN pId INT
```

---

# OUT Parameter

Returns a value.

Example

```sql
DELIMITER $$

CREATE PROCEDURE StudentCount
(
OUT Total INT
)
BEGIN

SELECT COUNT(*)
INTO Total
FROM Student;

END $$

DELIMITER ;
```

Execute

```sql
CALL StudentCount(@Total);

SELECT @Total;
```

---

# INOUT Parameter

Works as both input and output.

```sql
DELIMITER $$

CREATE PROCEDURE DoubleNumber
(
INOUT Num INT
)
BEGIN

SET Num = Num * 2;

END $$

DELIMITER ;
```

Execute

```sql
SET @Num = 10;

CALL DoubleNumber(@Num);

SELECT @Num;
```

Output

```
20
```

