# Interview Questions

## 1. What is a Stored Procedure?

A Stored Procedure is a precompiled collection of SQL statements stored inside the database.

---

## 2. Why do we use Stored Procedures?

- Performance
- Security
- Reusability
- Maintenance

---

## 3. Difference between Procedure and Function?

| Procedure | Function |
|------------|----------|
| Can return multiple values | Returns one value |
| Can use INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE | Mostly used for calculations |
| Called using CALL | Used inside SELECT |

---

## 4. What are Parameter Types?

- IN
- OUT
- INOUT

---

## 5. Why use DELIMITER?

Because procedures contain multiple SQL statements ending with `;`. Changing the delimiter allows MySQL to treat the entire procedure as one statement.

